[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753968304","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104633#issuecomment-2753968304","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104633","id":2753968304,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kJjiw","user":{"login":"WouterB15","id":33959438,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTU5NDM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33959438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15","html_url":"https://github.com/WouterB15","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T10:40:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T10:41:59Z","body":"According to the [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_rigidbody3d.html#class-rigidbody3d-method-apply-impulse) `apply_impulse()` is not meant to be applied every physics frame. For that you want to use `apply_force()` instead.\nAnd yes, you should use the global_transform for getting the force direction.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753968304/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2756214589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104633#issuecomment-2756214589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104633","id":2756214589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kSH89","user":{"login":"CsloudX","id":35988767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTg4NzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35988767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX","html_url":"https://github.com/CsloudX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-27T01:36:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T01:36:25Z","body":"I'm also test the `apply_force()`, it was the same strange behavior.\nfor me, like when the body was not rotate, it isright.\nbut when the body rotated, the force position like alway on center.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2756214589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2757251650","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104633#issuecomment-2757251650","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104633","id":2757251650,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kWFJC","user":{"login":"WouterB15","id":33959438,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTU5NDM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33959438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15","html_url":"https://github.com/WouterB15","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WouterB15/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-27T09:02:36Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T09:04:30Z","body":"Made it work as expected. I did a couple things:\n\n- Your impulse components 2 and 3 were flipped. Number 2 was facing right, but triggered when pressing left and vice versa. I flipped them.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4ea9e47a-4bc2-46c8-919a-ba60d47232a8)\n\n- Both `apply_force()` and `apply_impulse()` take a position argument on where to find the force. The docs say this is in the offset in **global** coordinates. Passing in the position of the impulse component seems correct, but is not. The local position (i.e. the `position` property) does not change when the parent rotates, meaning if you use that as the force position it will always apply the force in the same position, regardless of the parent rotation.\nTo fix this, you need to subtract the parent global position from the impulse component global position in order to get the offset in _global coordinates_. Like so:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b376f104-8e93-4c58-8ad2-b102d139d137)\n\nI've also added the `force`  variable, which you can edit in the inspector.\n\n- Lastly, if you plan to keep this perspective (that being, 2d in a 3d space), I recommend turning on Axis Lock for `Linear Z` and `Angular X`. This prevents the rigid body from floating away or closer to the camera, and also rotating away or towards the camera. But this of course depends on whatever you want to do with the game.\nWith the current setup this makes no difference, but if you introduce an object where the center of mass is no longer on the same plane as where the forces are applied, you'll start spinning in directions you don't expect.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/449da6ab-01c9-4474-a9ab-934f60b9924a)\n\nAs this is not an engine bug, I think it's safe to say you can close the issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2757251650/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759965955","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104633#issuecomment-2759965955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104633","id":2759965955,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kgb0D","user":{"login":"CsloudX","id":35988767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTg4NzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35988767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX","html_url":"https://github.com/CsloudX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T01:56:14Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T01:56:14Z","body":"@WouterB15 Oh, thanks so much! ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759965955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]